## Activity 4: Data Quality and Risk Analysis

| Data Item | Risk | Business Impact | Prevention Strategy |
|---|---|---|---|
| Product Price | Incorrect value entered by admin | Customers over/undercharged; refund disputes and lost trust | Input validation (numeric, min/max), confirmation step before publishing price changes |
| Product Stock Level | Not decremented after a sale, or entered incorrectly | Overselling out-of-stock items; customer complaints and refunds | Real-time stock decrement on order confirmation; low-stock alerts for admin |
| Customer Email | Mistyped or invalid on contact/registration form | Enquiry responses and order confirmations never reach the customer | Email format validation on submit; confirmation email with retry prompt |
| Customer Password | Stored in plain text or with weak hashing | Full account compromise if the database is breached | Hash with bcrypt/argon2, salted; never log or display raw passwords |
| Cart Total | Miscalculated due to rounding or promo-code bugs | Financial loss to the business or customer disputes at checkout | Server-side recalculation before payment is charged; automated unit tests for pricing logic |
| Product Category | Missing or inconsistent category assigned | Products become undiscoverable, reducing sales through filters/nav | Mandatory field with a fixed dropdown list rather than free text |
| User Role | Assigned incorrectly (e.g. customer given admin rights) | Unauthorised access to admin product/order management | Role-based access control; only existing admins can grant admin role |
| Shipping Address | Incomplete or incorrect address entered at checkout | Failed deliveries, reshipping cost, and customer dissatisfaction | Address validation/autocomplete; required-field checks before order submission |
| Session / Auth Token | Token does not expire or is stored insecurely (e.g. localStorage) | Session hijacking or account takeover | Short expiry, HttpOnly secure cookies, HTTPS enforced site-wide |
| Payment Status | Not updated promptly after a successful payment | Customer confusion, support overload, possible duplicate charges | Automated status update via payment gateway webhook rather than manual entry |
| Contact/Enquiry Message | No spam or input validation on the form | Wasted staff time on spam; genuine enquiries missed or delayed | Basic input sanitisation, simple bot-check (e.g. honeypot field or CAPTCHA) |

