## Activity 5: Planning for Future Development

**What information should be stored permanently?**
Product records (name, description, SKU history), completed order records and payment status, and customer accounts should be retained permanently for record-keeping, customer support and financial/tax reporting, even after an order is fulfilled.

**What information changes frequently?**
Stock levels, product pricing/promotions, cart contents and order/delivery status change frequently — stock and cart data in particular can change within seconds during checkout, so these need real-time updates rather than cached values.

**What information should be restricted to administrators?**
Revenue and sales statistics, full customer lists, other customers' order details, and the ability to edit stock/price/category should be restricted to the admin role only, enforced through role-based access control rather than hiding buttons in the UI.

**What information should be included in future reports?**
Reports should include total orders and revenue over time, best-selling products and categories, low-stock alerts, and enquiry volume/response times — giving the client visibility into both sales performance and customer service quality.

**What information might be required in Capstone B Version 2?**
Version 2 could require customer order history and wishlists, product reviews/ratings, discount/promotion codes, multiple shipping addresses per customer, and refund/return records — all of which should be considered now so the Capstone B database schema can accommodate them without a costly redesign.

